    "result_text": "Green. Version 2 of the owner identity is implemented and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What changed\n\n**Version-2 region code inside the identifiers** \u2014 new `RegionCode` helper derives the region code with the plain region plus a fixed `\"V2\"` tag mixed in. It's threaded into all three identifiers so every one changes and no v1 value recurs:\n- `AssignMemberId` \u2014 `REGION` segment is now `RegionCode.v2(city, postcode)` (e.g. `NSWV2261A2B3C4D5`).\n- `HouseholdId` \u2014 hashes `regionV2 + '|' + normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (region derived from postcode alone, so the same-lastName-and-postcode household invariant is preserved).\n- `IdentityKey` \u2014 now takes `postcode` and hashes `regionV2 + '|' + \u2026`; the three callers (`OwnerMapper`, `RejectDuplicateOwner`, `DetectPossibleDuplicate`) pass it consistently, so duplicate detection still matches.\n\n**`locality` stays plain** \u2014 the mapper now derives `locality`, `timezone` and `ownerSegment` directly from the plain region `Locality.of(city, postcode)` (decoupled from the memberId, whose region now carries `V2`). The dead `Locality.ofMemberId` was removed. The `\"V2\"` tag appears only inside the identifiers.\n\n**Response shape (v2)** \u2014 in `openapi.yml`: added top-level integer `apiVersion` (2), added an `OwnerIdentity` schema, and moved `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey` under a nested `identity` object (removed from top level). `OwnerMapper` maps `identity.*` and `apiVersion`.\n\n**Audit schema v2** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent` gained `schemaVersion` (`= 2`) and `ownerSegment`; `AuditOwnerCreated` emits both, with the segment recomputed from the plain region so no `V2` leaks. Observed at runtime: `{\"schemaVersion\":2,\u2026,\"memberId\":\"NSWV22716E6609E7\",\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec's phrase *\"the region code used inside the identifiers, the householdId, the identityKey and the memberId\"* I read as \"the region code, which each identifier now embeds in its v2 form.\" That meant adding a region component to `householdId` and `identityKey` (previously region-free). This changes their derivation and, for `identityKey`, means two owners with matching phone/email/surname but different postcodes are no longer hard duplicates \u2014 a deliberate behavior change consistent with *\"several existing behaviours \u2026 change at once.\"* No test pins the old cross-postcode duplicate behavior, and the only enforced contract (the structural `apiVersion`/nested-`identity` test) passes.",
