    "probe_text": "I've read the full pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`) and every function class it wires together. Here is the complete ordered list of what happens when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Precondition\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the whole endpoint is guarded by `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` (`composition.authorize`). Failing this yields a 403 before any step runs.\n\nEvery step below runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole pipeline commits once at the end.\n\n## The pipeline, in order\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** *(side-effect / short-circuit)* \u2014 Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If present, non-blank, and already recorded against an existing owner, it **responds 200 OK with that original owner and stops** (no create). Otherwise takes the `proceed` branch. A missing/blank key always proceeds.\n\n**2. `NormalizeAddress`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 The single step that binds the request body (`@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, no `@Valid`, so bean-validation annotations do **not** run). Normalizes the address to canonical form (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations). Prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` when `addressLine1` is non-blank (composing them into flat `address`); otherwise normalizes the flat `address`. Republishes the DTO as a variable for later steps.\n\n**3. `RequireOwnerFields`** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 Rejects if any mandatory field is missing/blank: `firstName`, `lastName`, address (either `addressLine1` or flat `address`), `city`, `telephone`. Throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n\n**4. `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 If `registrationDate` is supplied and later than the server's current date, throws `FutureRegistrationDateException`. Absent date is allowed.\n\n**5. `ValidatePostcode`** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 Optional `postcode`; when present it must be exactly 4 digits, and for a city with a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in range. Malformed/out-of-range throws `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n\n**6. `NormalizeTelephone`** *(side-effect + validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 Normalizes telephone to E.164 (defaults `+61`, drops a leading `0`, strips separators, requires 8\u201315 digits), writing it back onto the DTO. Invalid numbers throw `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n**7. `NormalizeEmail`** *(side-effect + validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 Optional `email`; if present, must be syntactically valid then is trimmed and lower-cased back onto the DTO. Invalid throws `InvalidEmailException`.\n\n**8. `RejectDisposableEmailDomain`** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 If the email's domain is on the disposable-domain blocklist, throws `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n\n**9. `RejectDuplicateOwner`** *(validation \u2192 409)* \u2014 Computes an `IdentityKey` (SHA-256 over normalized telephone + lower email + soundex(lastName), also using postcode) and rejects if it collides with any existing non-soft-deleted owner. **Bypassed** when the request sets `sharesHousehold=true`. Throws `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n\n**10. `RejectCityAtCapacity`** *(validation \u2192 409)* \u2014 Rejects if the owner's city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed match). Throws `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n**11. `RejectOverDailyLimit`** *(validation \u2192 429)* \u2014 Rejects if \u2265 100 owners already exist for the effective, business-day-adjusted registration date. Throws `DailyLimitExceededException`.\n\n**12. `BuildOwner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity; sets `registrationDate` (defaulting to today when absent) rolled forward off weekends to the next business day.\n\n**13. `AssignMemberId`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Computes `memberId` as `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (v2 region code, fiscal-year, SHA-256 hash of telephone+lastName, Luhn check digit), appending `-<n>` to resolve collisions with existing member ids.\n\n**14. `CountNamesakes`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**15. `CountHousehold`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `householdSize` = existing owners in the same `HouseholdId` (last name + postcode) plus this one.\n\n**16. `AssignMembershipLevel`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Computes `membershipPoints` (email +2, no namesakes +1, household \u22653 +2, tenure \u22651 fiscal year +3) and derives numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20134).\n\n**17. `CapMembershipLevel`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Caps `membershipLevel` to at most one above the highest existing level in the same household.\n\n**18. `FlagBulkSignup`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `bulkSignupWarning=true` when > 80 owners already exist for this registration day.\n\n**19. `FlagCityCapacityWarning`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `capacityWarning=true` when the city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the cap of 50).\n\n**20. `DetectPossibleDuplicate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Soft-match: sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (lowest matching id) when a non-deleted owner shares soundex(lastName) + postcode but a *different* identity key. Skipped (flags cleared) when `sharesHousehold=true`.\n\n**21. `SaveOwner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Persists the owner via the repository (assigns its id).\n\n**22. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 If the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records key \u2192 new owner id for future replays.\n\n**23. `AuditOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Emits two `AUDIT` log entries: a human-readable line and a JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (monotonic seq, id, memberId, level, segment).\n\n**24. `NotifyWelcome`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Emits a `NOTIFY` log line (welcome notification) with the owner id and memberId.\n\n**25. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(response)* \u2014 Maps to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Notes\n- Validation ordering is deliberate: body normalization \u2192 required fields \u2192 cheap field validations \u2192 duplicate/capacity/limit checks \u2192 build/enrich \u2192 persist \u2192 audit/notify \u2192 respond.\n- Because step 2 binds `@RequestBody` **without** `@Valid`, DTO bean-validation constraints are not enforced; all validation is the explicit steps above.\n- Escalation handlers under `officefloor/escalation/` map each thrown exception to its status code (400/409/429), and there are catch-alls for `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, `DataIntegrityViolationException`, and `Exception`."
